cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Reflex-2, please cite it as below."
title: "Reflex-2: fast, local judgments on video with a 740M open embedding model"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Suzuki
    given-names: Gosuke
    affiliation: Suzuki Shoten
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-09
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/matu79go/reflex-2"
url: "https://huggingface.co/matu79go/Reflex-2"
abstract: >-
  Reflex-2 judges camera video, images and audio on local hardware. It embeds a clip
  into one vector with Google EmbeddingGemma 2 (740M parameters, unmodified) and reads
  that vector with small logistic-regression heads trained from labelled examples in
  seconds. On fall detection (GMDCSA24, leave-one-person-out) it reaches 95.7% balanced
  accuracy at 0.3 s per clip on one GPU; on the same 40 clips it scores 97.5% against
  85.0% for Gemini 3.8 Flash, which takes 6.95 s per clip through its API.
keywords:
  - video classification
  - fall detection
  - embedding model
  - edge AI
  - Gemma
